same – fixed arrangement in the future.

00:13:17.962 --> 00:13:21.277
Okay, so let’s summarize.
So, Present Simple tense.

00:13:21.436 --> 00:13:24.854
We use the Present Simple,
we’ll start with Present Simple,

00:13:24.965 --> 00:13:26.965
with habits or routines.

00:13:27.148 --> 00:13:29.699
So: “I leave my house
early every morning.”

00:13:29.827 --> 00:13:32.639
Habits – that’s something
that I do regularly.

00:13:32.782 --> 00:13:37.016
“I do yoga in the morning”,
for example. Let’s move on.

00:13:37.278 --> 00:13:39.350
So - permanent state or situations.

00:13:39.434 --> 00:13:42.156
“Does he work in the bank? Yes, he does.”

00:13:42.291 --> 00:13:45.041
So, permanent – стабільне. Okay?

00:13:45.262 --> 00:13:51.178
“Does he work as a teacher? Yes,
she is a teacher”, for example. Okay.

00:13:51.611 --> 00:13:52.944
Let’s move on.

00:13:54.518 --> 00:13:59.038
So - programmes and timetables.
“The gym doesn’t open on Saturdays.”

00:13:59.195 --> 00:14:05.156
Or, for example, “My
flight departs at 5 o'clock –

00:14:05.307 --> 00:14:06.890
this is scheduled”.

00:14:07.190 --> 00:14:13.290
Okay. And – general
truth or laws of nature.

00:14:13.706 --> 00:14:17.082
“In winter it snows in
the mountains”. Okay?

00:14:17.185 --> 00:14:21.092
Okay? Or, for example: “It’s
really hot in summer”. Right?

00:14:21.283 --> 00:14:24.178
Or: “The water boils at 100 degrees”.

00:14:24.290 --> 00:14:25.368
- General truth.

00:14:25.472 --> 00:14:29.747
- General truth. Good? Let’s
have a look at the trigger words.

00:14:29.832 --> 00:14:34.251
Trigger words – these are the words
that we see the word and we understand –

00:14:34.336 --> 00:14:35.706
this is Present Simple.

00:14:35.791 --> 00:14:36.627
- Like usual.

00:14:36.746 --> 00:14:37.611
- Okay.

00:14:37.762 --> 00:14:38.603
- Every day.

00:14:38.701 --> 00:14:39.534
- Yes.

00:14:41.157 --> 00:14:42.160
- That’s all.

00:14:42.244 --> 00:14:47.858
- Sometimes. Have a look: every
hour, every day,

00:14:48.711 --> 00:14:49.794
every Monday.

00:14:49.893 --> 00:14:50.973
- Every something.

00:14:51.093 --> 00:14:55.008
- Yes, every Sunday, every summer. Okay?

00:14:55.683 --> 00:14:58.626
In the morning, in the
afternoon, in the evening.

00:14:58.770 --> 00:15:04.240
What else? At night, at the
weekend, at 5 o'clock. Good.

00:15:05.180 --> 00:15:08.817
On Monday on Friday, on
Saturday and so on and so forth.

00:15:08.921 --> 00:15:11.583
We see these words –
we immediately understand

00:15:11.742 --> 00:15:14.966
that this is Present Simple tense. Okay.

00:15:15.151 --> 00:15:17.383
Now, let’s revise the formation.

00:15:17.572 --> 00:15:21.655
How do we make positive,
negative and questions?

00:15:21.877 --> 00:15:24.067
Positive sentence, negative sentence.

00:15:24.152 --> 00:15:26.638
- З якого слова ми
починаємо будувати, так?

00:15:26.782 --> 00:15:30.948
- Yeah, how we make up
sentences? Do you remember?

00:15:31.153 --> 00:15:34.242
- If you will show
example for us, we’ll see.

00:15:34.327 --> 00:15:36.799
- Yes, I’ll help you.

00:15:36.887 --> 00:15:38.721
- Ah, these ones, yes.

00:15:38.891 --> 00:15:41.209
Yes. So, these are positive sentences.

00:15:41.304 --> 00:15:46.618
With I and we, we just take the subject
– підмет – and then the verb. Right?

00:15:46.777 --> 00:15:52.291
I play football. I cook breakfast,
we play football, we cook breakfast.

00:15:52.442 --> 00:15:56.442
But the difference with
he, she, it. So, we add…

00:15:57.107 --> 00:15:58.115
- Закінчення -s.

00:15:58.320 --> 00:16:03.002
- Yes. Negative – you
see, the verb is the same.

00:16:03.193 --> 00:16:05.934
But we have don’t or doesn’t.

00:16:06.157 --> 00:16:10.240
This is the auxiliary verb
– допоміжне дієслово.

00:16:10.463 --> 00:16:14.796
And questions. So, we
put the auxiliary verb first.

00:16:15.006 --> 00:16:19.924
Do I play? Does he play?
Or - do we play? Okay?

00:16:20.401 --> 00:16:24.890
So, let’s summarize.
Positive – no auxiliary.

00:16:25.073 --> 00:16:29.838
Negative and question – we
have auxiliary – do or does. Okay?

00:16:30.693 --> 00:16:33.610
Let’s move on. Present Continuous.

00:16:33.892 --> 00:16:37.966
This is a boring part but let’s make it.

00:16:38.660 --> 00:16:42.408
So, we use Present Continuous
with actions happening now.

00:16:42.504 --> 00:16:44.566
We are talking now. Yes?

00:16:44.650 --> 00:16:48.089
“We are making
video-lesson for the students”.

00:16:48.272 --> 00:16:52.244
This is happening now. “We
are exercising a lot these days”.

00:16:52.435 --> 00:16:56.329
Why these days? Because
this is not only happening now

00:16:56.483 --> 00:17:00.457
but around now – те, що
відбувається не тільки зараз,

00:17:00.542 --> 00:17:04.345
в момент мовлення, а й ще час
трохи більший, ніж момент мовлення.

00:17:04.430 --> 00:17:06.654
- So, it will start and will finish.

00:17:06.756 --> 00:17:12.154
- It is still in process. These days.
So, we are staying home these days.

00:17:12.337 --> 00:17:15.614
Correct? We started and
we are still staying homes.

00:17:15.796 --> 00:17:18.701
We are staying homes these days. Good.

00:17:18.908 --> 00:17:21.714
Fixed future arrangements.
Do you remember

00:17:21.881 --> 00:17:28.464
“I'm going to Bath”. So, “I'm
not visiting gym tomorrow”…

00:17:28.579 --> 00:17:30.477
- … because I'm going to Bath.

00:17:30.635 --> 00:17:36.038
- Yes, “because I'm going to Bath” or “I'm
not going to the mall”.

00:17:37.038 --> 00:17:38.371
Correct as well.

00:17:38.732 --> 00:17:42.330
Good. Currently changing
and developing situations

00:17:42.513 --> 00:17:44.929
That is something that keeps on changing.

00:17:45.311 --> 00:17:47.318
“My English is improving”.

00:17:47.430 --> 00:17:51.833
“My yoga is improving”. Or: “My
bank account is getting down”.

00:17:51.961 --> 00:17:53.651
- Become better, yeah?

00:17:53.762 --> 00:18:00.012
- Become better, yes, changing situation.
Okay, we use Continuous as well.

00:18:00.304 --> 00:18:05.267
And the last thing – with always or
constantly to express annoyance.

00:18:05.434 --> 00:18:09.907
So, we are annoyed. “Why
are you doing this all the time”?

00:18:09.997 --> 00:18:11.950
So, have a look at this example.

00:18:12.046 --> 00:18:17.629
The person is listening to music
very loud and it drives me crazy.

00:18:17.906 --> 00:18:24.317
So, I want to express my annoyance. “You
are always playing your music too loud”.

00:18:24.725 --> 00:18:30.261
In order to express this annoyance – “you
are always playing your music too loud” –

00:18:30.539 --> 00:18:32.852
you can say this, Continuous. Okay?

00:18:32.995 --> 00:18:35.490
- It’s like only rule
you have to remember.

00:18:35.610 --> 00:18:38.741
- Yes, these are the rules
that you need to remember.

00:18:39.012 --> 00:18:40.262
Trigger words?

00:18:41.125 --> 00:18:43.125
Not always or every day.

00:18:43.263 --> 00:18:44.096
- Now?

00:18:44.382 --> 00:18:46.299
- Now, good. What else?

00:18:48.148 --> 00:18:49.647
Tomorrow? No?

00:18:49.743 --> 00:18:54.040
- No, these days, at the
moment and nowadays.

00:18:54.278 --> 00:18:58.474
Nowadays is similar to these days
and at the moment is similar to now.

00:18:58.586 --> 00:19:04.622
Okay? So, simply, this is happening now
and we are talking about this. Formation.

00:19:04.829 --> 00:19:08.025
Let’s have a look. Positive
sentences, we have:

00:19:08.407 --> 00:19:15.339
I – am; he, she, it – is; you,
we, they – are. Fantastic.

00:19:15.929 --> 00:19:19.096
And we have -ing ending all the time.

00:19:19.750 --> 00:19:24.883
So, the thing that is changing is actually
to be verb. Am, is, are. Am, is, are.

00:19:25.003 --> 00:19:27.926
Am, is, are. Only this
thing changes. Okay?

00:19:28.116 --> 00:19:28.949
- Yes.

00:19:29.086 --> 00:19:32.208
- Good. So, now it’s quiz-time.

00:19:32.305 --> 00:19:34.472
- Yay! Game! I like games.

00:19:34.775 --> 00:19:40.442
- This is not a game. A game is
going to be a bit later. Quiz-time!

00:19:41.749 --> 00:19:48.583
So, I'm going to check you. Have a look
at this sentence. Is this correct or not?

00:19:49.029 --> 00:19:50.719
He plays tennis every day.

00:19:50.804 --> 00:19:52.002
- Yes, it’s correct.

00:19:52.086 --> 00:19:56.219
- Correct, let’s check.
Bravo! It is correct. Number 2.

00:19:58.482 --> 00:20:00.148
He driving home now.

00:20:00.240 --> 00:20:02.324
- He is driving home now.

00:20:02.598 --> 00:20:08.764
- Let’s check. So, it’s not correct. He
is driving home now. And one more.

00:20:10.106 --> 00:20:11.023
- They are…

00:20:12.458 --> 00:20:15.207
- They don’t drive.

00:20:15.684 --> 00:20:22.618
- Okay, they don’t drive to work on
Fridays. Yes, amazing! Fantastic students.

00:20:23.584 --> 00:20:27.267
Okay, let’s have some practice.
So, we have two people talking.

00:20:27.355 --> 00:20:28.355
- Yes, okay.

00:20:28.513 --> 00:20:31.638
- Jane and Mona, for
example. Or Svitlana and Fima.

00:20:31.813 --> 00:20:35.474
And we have to open the
brackets. Simply to ask the question.

00:20:35.649 --> 00:20:40.798
Have a look. La-la-la… to
work every day. Not always.

00:20:40.957 --> 00:20:46.405
This week, he… the train into the
city because the traffic is so bad.

00:20:46.652 --> 00:20:48.574
Let’s start with number 1.

00:20:48.757 --> 00:20:51.180
- Does your dad drive to work every day?

00:20:51.307 --> 00:20:56.741
- Yes. We have every day.
So, this is Present Simple.

00:20:57.157 --> 00:21:00.365
Does your dad drive home
every day? Not always.

00:21:00.484 --> 00:21:03.233
This week – Svitlana, maybe you try?

00:21:03.392 --> 00:21:09.414
- This week he is take the
train… Takes? He takes! No?

00:21:09.589 --> 00:21:10.493
- Are you sure?

00:21:10.578 --> 00:21:11.420
- He is…

00:21:11.504 --> 00:21:13.910
- So, have a look. This is not always.

00:21:14.284 --> 00:21:17.844
This is this week. So,
this is a changing situation.

00:21:21.487 --> 00:21:23.294
- He is taking.

00:21:23.469 --> 00:21:24.312
- Bravo.

00:21:24.397 --> 00:21:25.761
- Oh, -ing, закінчення.

00:21:25.876 --> 00:21:29.021
- Okay, so, can you read
the whole sentence, please?

00:21:29.119 --> 00:21:31.406
- Not always. This week.

00:21:31.605 --> 00:21:37.594
He is taking the train into the
city because the traffic is so bad.

00:21:37.789 --> 00:21:39.503
- She is amazing, isn’t she?

00:21:40.090 --> 00:21:44.263
Okay, let’s move on.
One more phrase for you.

00:21:44.438 --> 00:21:47.588
…Mia/usually study in the evening?

00:21:47.836 --> 00:21:53.579
Oh yes. Actually, she…
her homework right now.

00:21:56.465 --> 00:22:01.754
- Does Mia usually study in the evening?

00:22:01.976 --> 00:22:05.209
- Because we have in the
evening, right. That’s why

00:22:05.361 --> 00:22:10.017
“Does Mia usually study in the
evening?”. Okay, and the second one?

00:22:10.335 --> 00:22:15.499
- Oh yes. Actually, she is studies…

00:22:16.241 --> 00:22:17.575
Ah, she’s doing.

00:22:17.717 --> 00:22:19.004
- We have right now.

00:22:19.132 --> 00:22:21.569
- She is doing her homework right now.

00:22:21.760 --> 00:22:25.758
- Let’s check. Yes, she is
doing her homework right now.

00:22:25.869 --> 00:22:30.540
- Все, я зрозуміла. В першому ти вставляєш
does, а потім я -ing закінчую. І все!

00:22:30.734 --> 00:22:35.817
- It doesn’t work like this!
Always watch for trigger words.

00:22:35.916 --> 00:22:39.215
In yellow – in the evening.
What's this – in the evening?

00:22:39.834 --> 00:22:43.862
Try to remember – in the evening,
trigger words, we had every hour,

00:22:43.997 --> 00:22:49.867
every week, in the morning. Ah, in
the evening – so this is Present Simple.

00:22:49.955 --> 00:22:50.788
Right now?

00:22:50.873 --> 00:22:52.124
- Present Continuous.

00:22:52.227 --> 00:22:57.010
- Bravo! Okay. So, you
always watch for trigger words.

00:22:57.193 --> 00:23:01.839
This will help you.
Now, let’s play a game!

00:23:01.991 --> 00:23:03.360
- Let’s play a game!

00:23:03.463 --> 00:23:04.827
- Let’s play a game?

00:23:05.170 --> 00:23:10.986
- So, do you like knots and
crosses game? You don’t like it?

00:23:12.887 --> 00:23:14.521
- No, we like it.

00:23:14.638 --> 00:23:17.653
- Excuse me, one more
time, how it… what's the name?

00:23:17.804 --> 00:23:23.534
- Knots and crosses. Knots. And crosses.
This is a knot. And this is a cross.

00:23:23.644 --> 00:23:30.641
Knots and crosses. There is one more
name for it. It’s called “tic-tac-toe”.

00:23:31.272 --> 00:23:33.597
“Tic-tac-toe” – the name of the game.

00:23:33.733 --> 00:23:37.442
But we got to the name “knots
and crosses”, this is easier.

00:23:37.562 --> 00:23:40.843
So, have a look. Nine spaces

00:23:41.441 --> 00:23:44.777
Here we have positive sentence.

00:23:44.976 --> 00:23:48.524
Negative sentence. Question.

00:23:49.527 --> 00:23:50.515
- Yes.

00:23:50.599 --> 00:23:53.433
- And here we have she,

00:23:54.183 --> 00:23:56.826
I and we.

00:23:58.473 --> 00:24:04.177
So, if I want to put my
cross or a knot here,

00:24:04.550 --> 00:24:08.594
I need to say a sentence.
Negative sentence with she.

00:24:09.042 --> 00:24:15.751
And we’ll use Present Simple. So,
the Present Simple with she will be like:

00:24:16.278 --> 00:24:20.312
“She doesn’t like milk” or
“She doesn’t go to the gym”.

00:24:20.680 --> 00:24:21.513
-Yes.

00:24:21.983 --> 00:24:25.987
- Okay. If I want to put it here,
Fima, positive sentence with we,

00:24:26.082 --> 00:24:28.114
give me an example, please.

00:24:28.265 --> 00:24:30.515
The present Simple with we.

00:24:30.746 --> 00:24:32.365
- We like play football…

00:24:32.540 --> 00:24:34.433
- Yes, we like playing football.

00:24:34.544 --> 00:24:36.036
- Every day, every night.

00:24:36.124 --> 00:24:40.624
- Yes. Svitlana, if I want
to ask a question with she?

00:24:40.906 --> 00:24:44.933
- Does she… Fima!

00:24:45.053 --> 00:24:50.053
- We have only one, does she
like play football every night?

00:24:50.249 --> 00:24:52.895
- Does she like playing
football every night!

00:24:52.999 --> 00:24:55.460
Okay, so, ladies go
first, don’t you mind?

00:24:55.651 --> 00:24:56.568
- Oh my god!

00:24:56.751 --> 00:25:00.467
- So, Svitlana, you choose. What
do you want? A knot or a cross?

00:25:00.552 --> 00:25:02.562
- I always win with a cross.

00:25:02.690 --> 00:25:07.235
- A cross, because cross is always
start. So, you will have a cross.

00:25:07.523 --> 00:25:10.620
Fima, you’ve got a knot. Cross is start.

00:25:10.819 --> 00:25:13.595
Svitlana, where would
you like to put you cross?

00:25:16.144 --> 00:25:18.227
Okay, give me a sentence.

00:25:18.781 --> 00:25:24.101
- I always try to be beautiful?

00:25:24.247 --> 00:25:29.363
- This is nice, okay. So, your
cross is here. Fima, your turn.

00:25:29.681 --> 00:25:32.381
- I don’t like listening to music.

00:25:32.500 --> 00:25:33.500
- Fantastic.

00:25:33.769 --> 00:25:37.522
- You have a big problem. You
have a big problem in your life.

00:25:37.606 --> 00:25:41.074
- You have a big problem
because I have no in the sentence.

00:25:41.186 --> 00:25:47.166
- I guess you're banned. Okay, so,
Svitlana, continue. Your second sentence.

00:25:47.318 --> 00:25:52.870
- She… She always takes the breakfast on…

00:25:53.174 --> 00:25:54.099
- As.

00:25:54.183 --> 00:25:55.174
- As a takeaway.

00:25:55.286 --> 00:25:56.119
- Bravo!

00:25:57.498 --> 00:25:58.331
- Fima?

00:25:58.570 --> 00:26:04.168
- I think there was some
help from you, okay, okay.

00:26:05.901 --> 00:26:10.707
We like when

00:26:12.705 --> 00:26:14.951
boys are champions.

00:26:15.086 --> 00:26:19.668
- Wow, this is a really nice
sentence. Boys are the champions.

00:26:19.859 --> 00:26:22.442
We are the champions! Svitlana?

00:26:22.620 --> 00:26:28.138
- Does she play football in the evening?

00:26:28.505 --> 00:26:31.507
- Good. Fima?

00:26:31.611 --> 00:26:35.392
- I think that she doesn’t like
playing football in the evening.

00:26:35.512 --> 00:26:38.277
- Good, okay. That’s serious.

00:26:38.762 --> 00:26:44.463
- We… We don’t like fake news.

00:26:44.582 --> 00:26:49.239
- We don’t like fake news! No,
we don’t like fake news, I agree.

00:26:50.562 --> 00:26:52.966
- It doesn’t matter but…

00:26:53.078 --> 00:26:55.245
- We need to finish, okay.

00:26:55.708 --> 00:26:59.041
- Does we like friendship between girls?

00:26:59.188 --> 00:27:00.938
- Ooh, again, please?

00:27:01.544 --> 00:27:04.453
- Do we like friendship
between girls and boys?

00:27:04.537 --> 00:27:09.872
- Okay, so, it’s like this. And for
you, Svitlana, just finish the sentence.

00:27:09.999 --> 00:27:10.832
- For fun.

00:27:11.527 --> 00:27:15.903
Do I take fitness in the morning?

00:27:16.054 --> 00:27:19.886
- Do I have a fitness class in
the morning? Yeah, like this.

00:27:21.847 --> 00:27:26.637
So, there is no winner.
There is a tie. We call it a tie.

00:27:26.722 --> 00:27:27.560
- Oh.

00:27:27.647 --> 00:27:28.504
- Yes, нічия.

00:27:28.616 --> 00:27:35.282
- Or a draw – нічия – yes. We don’t say
friendship, we call it a tie or a draw.

00:27:36.027 --> 00:27:42.829
So, your homework guys. Write 5
sentences using the Present Simple

00:27:42.941 --> 00:27:47.274
and 5 sentences using the
Present Continuous. Okay?

00:27:47.699 --> 00:27:52.204
And there is a bell. Unfortunately,
we have to finish the lesson.

00:27:52.403 --> 00:27:53.736
- Unfortunately.

00:27:53.879 --> 00:27:55.192
- Thank you very much.

00:27:55.295 --> 00:27:56.247
- It was cool.

00:27:56.359 --> 00:27:59.983
- Thank you so much it was
very fun and very… Пізнавально?…

00:28:00.491 --> 00:28:01.324
- Useful.

00:28:01.436 --> 00:28:02.292
- Useful!

00:28:02.396 --> 00:28:05.697
- Useful! Thank you very
much, see you next time!

00:28:10.885 --> 00:28:15.405
- Боже, це так хвилююче, я так не
нервувала навіть перед концертами своїми.

00:28:15.524 --> 00:28:18.733
- Сьогодні був простий
урок, але я помилився,

00:28:18.908 --> 00:28:21.020
мабуть, один-два рази я помилився.

00:28:21.219 --> 00:28:26.684
Тому що – це іноді занадто
просто і мозок виключається.

00:28:26.843 --> 00:28:30.627
Ну, ти думаєш: «А, я це зроблю
на 100%», а потім помиляєшся.

00:28:30.826 --> 00:28:37.742
- Цей урок надихнув мене під час, можливо,
карантину зайнятися англійською мовою.

00:28:41.971 --> 00:28:46.854
В Present Continuous
будується запитання так…

00:28:49.532 --> 00:28:50.365
Фіма!?

00:28:50.478 --> 00:28:57.442
Спочатку дієслово, тобто does
she play football in the evening?

00:28:59.064 --> 00:29:00.527
Playing!

00:29:01.609 --> 00:29:04.363
Is she? А is she? Як правильно, Фіма?

00:29:05.286 --> 00:29:09.321
Is she, okay. Is she playing
football in the evening?

00:29:09.504 --> 00:29:15.429
Every day? Right now. Cut!
Залиште ще Фімі, будь ласка!

00:29:15.988 --> 00:29:22.905
Now, at the moment and that’s all.

00:29:23.161 --> 00:29:28.153
I don’t remember all but
all these words mean “now”.

